  "derivation": "A twentieth-century French loanword, and the arrow French > Persian is exactly right. Persian ژیمناستیک žimnāstīk renders French gymnastique [ʒimnastik]: Persian ژ /ʒ/ is the regular substitute for French initial g- before i/y (pronounced [ʒ]), the French nasal-free -ast- is kept, and -ique is naturalised as -یک. Both dictionaries tag the word as French: Moʿin '[فر.]' and Dehkhoda '[فرانسوی] ورزش بدنی با اسبابهای مختلف از قبیل پارالل و بارفیکس و دارحلقه'. It is therefore not an inherited Iranian word at all but a borrowing that re-imports the Greek root into Persian — the mirror image of the inherited برهنه at node #3, which reaches Persian from the same PIE root by descent.",
